      "content": "i hear you on the social issues, but the committee is being pretty blunt about the \"risk profile\" of these neighborhoods. \n\nthey're looking at the high percentages of black and hispanic residents in 90502 and 90990 and saying that the cultural and social environment there is fundamentally different and harder to \"fix\" with just a building. they're basically asking if it's more realistic to assume that investment in those specific demographics will actually lead to \"stability,\" or if we should focus on the neighborhoods that already have a foundation of professional, middle-class values. \n\nfrom an urban planning standpoint, is there any data to suggest that certain demographic compositions are inherently more \"resistant\" to these types of community investments?",
